<title>CANADA: Canada agency details 1996/97 canola quality.</title>
<headline>Canada agency details 1996/97 canola quality.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Tuesday detailed the quality characteristics of No1 Canada canola harvested in the 1996/97 (Aug/July) crop year.</p>
<p>QUALITY PARAMETER		 1996    1995  1986-95 MEAN</p>
<p>Oil Content* (pct)		43.4    42.4    42.1</p>
<p>Protein Content* (pct)	  20.1    20.4    20.8</p>
<p>Oil-free Protein Content*(pct)38.2    38.1    38.5</p>
<p>Seed Chlorophyl (mg/kg)	 15	14	12</p>
<p>Free Fatty Acids (pct)	   0.2     0.2     0.3</p>
<p>Erucic Acid (pct in oil)	 0.4     0.3     0.5</p>
<p>Linolenic Acid (pct in oil)   10.4    11.0    10.7</p>
<p>Satrtd Fatty Acid (pct in oil) 6.8     6.8     6.4</p>
<p>Iodine Value		     115.0   117.0   117.0</p>
<p>*8.5 pct moisture basis</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
